{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485607742,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk0MDI1OTYyNQ=="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485607742,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk0MDI1OTYyNg=="},"added":["regression"],"removed":[]},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485629595,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50OTQwMzQzNDEz"},"title":"SSHManager is claiming to close connections that aren't open","was":"SSHManager is claiming to close connections that aren't open"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486668736,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODc0NzQ3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278747475"},"message":"FTR: Still happening with current master:\n\n````\n[DEBUG  ] Closing 2 SSH connections... \n[DEBUG  ] Running: ['ssh', '-O', 'stop', '-o', 'ControlPath=/home/mih/.cache/datalad/sockets/5f9602bf21b60aa7bd8bc12a64491f7a', 'git@github.com']\n| cwd: None \n[DEBUG  ] Failed to run ['ssh', '-O', 'stop', '-o', 'ControlPath=/home/mih/.cache/datalad/sockets/5f9602bf21b60aa7bd8bc12a64491f7a', 'git@github.com'] under None. Exit code=255. out= err=Control socket connect(/home/mih/.cache/datalad/sockets/5f9602bf21b60aa7bd8bc12a64491f7a): No such file or directory\n|  \n[DEBUG  ] Running: ['ssh', '-O', 'stop', '-o', 'ControlPath=/home/mih/.cache/datalad/sockets/747501b3584c118d95811f2c756f2a9f', 'kumo.ovgu.de']\n| cwd: None \n````\n\nThere is no SSH connection to github being opened before. There is no socket either, but it still wants to close one.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486711764,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg3NjQ1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278876453"},"message":"Well, from my point of view the issue is not, that `SSHManager` wants to close it. That's okay. It tries to make sure, all known connections are closed. The call fails, but this failure is intentionally ignored, since it's the desired result anyway. No error message, no exception - all fine.\n\nBut the question is: How the github connection got te be registered with the `SSHManager`, if you say it was never opened? I'd love to see how you produce this, because I don't believe it's true ;-)\nThere is exactly one way `SSHManager` gets to know about a connection and this is `SSHManager.get_connection()`. While it might not have been opened before, at the very least it was requested.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486712144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg3NzM3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278877378"},"message":"Now, that I wrote it, I'm confident to know where this comes from! ;-)\n\nThe repo in question is an annex and it has a github remote, right?\nTherefore, the connection instance was requested, but never opened.\n\nLeaves the question: What you want it to look like? Change the wording of the `Closing X connections ...` message? Take additional effort to first check whether it's open, instead of just trying to close and be fine with failure? Something else?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486713602,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg4MTA5OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278881099"},"message":"In particular as we are moving towards selective content publishing, I'd consider it suspicious to see a connection to a server being closed that I did not want to have anything published to.\n\nI would simply assume less in the messages, and perform cheap tests to avoid useless actions. At present, it knows that it could make an attempt to close a maximum of 2 connections (and logs that as if they would actually be in use), but users should not care about that. Moreover, it tries to close a connection although the socket file it knows about isn't actually present. Even if a connection to this server would anyhow be open, it could not be closed by the call it performs -- so why bother?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486715391,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg4NTk5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278885995"},"message":"\u003e but users should not care about that\n\nWell, yes. That's why it is logged at debug level.\n\nAs for \"cheap checks\": Of course we could check for the existence of the expected socket before. On the other hand this still wouldn't be a fully valid check on whether there's something to close - that's what `ssh -O check` is for. So, theoretically it could still technically fail to close the connection. And calling `ssh -O check` certainly isn't \"cheap\" in comparison to the actual close call. The other way around the failing call isn't something expensive, that's done several times. Right now it's a one time thing when the datalad process ends.\n\nTo me it looks more like the question \"What should be logged at what level?\" and/or \"What wording is least confusing and most informative?\"\nMay be all (or most) of the logging from `Runner` should not be done at debug level and the message from `SSHManager` should just read \"Closing SSH connections\" without mentioning a potentially confusing number?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486715548,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODg4NjQ0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1236#issuecomment-278886449"},"message":"All I am saying is: There is no point in calling `ssh -O stop` for a connection where there is no socket file.","files":null}]}